'''Chiefs Esports Club''' is an [[:category:Australia|Australian]] professional esports organization, which was well-known in other esports titles before entering the ''Rocket League'' scene in August of 2017.

The organization partnered with [https://www.helfie.ai/ Helfie] on January 9th 2025, branded as '''"Helfie Chiefs"'''.<ref name="chiefs25"/>

==History==
===Timeline===
{{tabs dynamic
|name1=2017
|name2=2018
|name3=2019
|name4=2020
|name5=2024
|name6=2025
|This=6
|content1=
*August 12th - [[Chiefs Esports Club]] acquires '''[[Billy Fan Club]]'''.<ref name="Chiefs eSports Club acquires BFC">{{cite web |url=http://chiefsesc.com/news/the-chiefs-welcome-rocket-league-squad|title=The Chiefs Welcome Rocket League Squad!|date=2017-08-12|author=[[Chiefs Esports Club]]}}</ref>
|content2=
*August 4th - [[Jake]] leaves [[Chiefs Esports Club]] and retires from competitive play.<ref name="Jake">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/JakeRL_/status/1025591707482476544|title=Leaving @ChiefsESC and retiring from professional Rocket League - Twitlonger later, but tldr we chillin - RLCS/RLRS teams interested in coaching, reach out via DM|date=2018-08-04|author=[[Jake]]}}</ref>
*August 17th - [[Kamii]] joins [[Chiefs Esports Club]].<ref name="Kamii">{{cite web|url=https://smash.gg/tournament/throwdown-rocket-league-oce-championship-18-s2/attendees/teams/2027252|title=Kamii in Chiefs Roster|date=2018-08-17}}</ref>
*October 1st - As [[Gfinity/Australia/Elite_Series/Season_2|Gfinity Elite Series Season 2]] approaches, [[Chiefs Esports Club]] acquires [[Requiem]], [[Kia]], and [[change]] for their roster, along with their main team.<ref name=GfinS2>[https://twitter.com/GfinityAU/status/1046701015569915904]</ref>
|content3=
*January 11th - [[Drippay]] leaves [[Chiefs Esports Club]] for '''[[Evil Geniuses]]'''.<ref name="drippay">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/EvilGeniuses/status/1083879038194724867|title=Roster Update: Evil Geniuses Rocket League — Welcome @DrippayRL|date=2019-01-11|author=[[Evil Geniuses]]}}</ref>
*January 26th - [[ZeN]] joins the team.<ref name="ZeN">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/ChiefsESC/status/1088966318504603650|title=The moment you've all been waiting for. Please welcome @ZeN_OCE to the Chiefs #RocketLeague squad!|date=2019-01-26|author=[[Chiefs Esports Club]]}}</ref>
*May 1st - '''[[Renegades]]''' acquires [[Chiefs Esports Club]]. [[Torsos]], [[ZeN]] and [[Kamii]] leave.<ref name="renegades">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/Renegades/status/1123362213291544576|title=Renegades Return to @RocketLeague!|date=2019-05-01|author=[[Renegades]]}}</ref>
*June 26th - '''[[ICON Esports]]''' announce their ownership of, and will be transferring their roster to, the [[Chiefs Esports Club]].<ref name="Chiefs2">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/CJCJ_RL/status/1143792163198656512|title=ICON acquires Chiefs Esports Club|date=2019-06-26|author=[[CJCJ]]}}</ref>
*July 21st - [[Hawk]] joins the team.<ref name="hawk">{{cite web|url=https://liquipedia.net/rocketleague/DreamHack/Pro_Circuit/2019/Montreal/Oceania/Closed_Qualifier|title=Hawk moves to Chiefs during the DH Montreal Closed Qualifier|date=2019-07-21}}</ref>
*August 3rd - [[shadey]] leaves [[Chiefs Esports Club]] and retires from competitive play.<ref name="shadey retires">{{cite web |url=https://twitter.com/ChiefsESC/status/1157554295589359616|title=Today we say farewell to Shadey|date=2019-08-03|author=[[Chiefs Esports Club]]}}</ref>
*September 13th - [[Drippay]] rejoins [[Chiefs Esports Club]].<ref name="drippay joins">{{cite web |url=https://twitter.com/ChiefsESC/status/1172434959526584323|title=The return. Welcome back @DrippayRL 💦 to the Chiefs @RocketLeague team. Time to get to work #WeAreChiefs🛡️|date=2019-09-13|author=[[Chiefs Esports Club]]}}</ref> [[Hawk]] leaves.<ref name="hawk leaves">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/ChiefsESC/status/1172435827906842626|title=We want to thank super-sub @Hawk_RL for his amazing performance in the @DreamHackRL Montreal Qualifiers and main tournament. You have a very bright future ahead!|date=2019-09-13|author=[[Chiefs Esports Club]]}}</ref>
|content4=
*February 5th - [[CJCJ]] leaves [[Chiefs Esports Club]] for '''[[Renegades]]'''.<ref name="cjcj">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/ChiefsESC/status/1224884036100751360|title=Today we say goodbye to the people's champ @CJCJ_RL 👑 We wish him all the best at his new home and we know he will keep doing his best to push OCE RL forward.|date=2020-02-05|author=[[Chiefs Esports Club]]}}</ref><ref name="rng cjcj">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/Renegades/status/1224894328214081536|title=We're ecstatic to announce the newest member of our Rocket League team. He's skilled. He's strong. He's talented... And now, he's a Renegade.|date=2020-02-05|author=[[Renegades]]}}</ref>
*February 6th - [[Express]] leaves [[Chiefs Esports Club]] for '''[[Ground Zero Gaming]]'''.<ref name="express">{{cite web|url=https://letsplay.live/tournaments/17807/team/115288/|title=Express to Ground Zero Gaming|date=2020-02-06}}</ref> [[Drippay]] leaves [[Chiefs Esports Club]] for '''[[Cringe Society]]'''.<ref name="cringe society">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/TorsosRL/status/1225360038627164161|title=Playing under Cringe Society (orgless) this season with:@DrippayRL, @SPYDOGE,@JakeRL(sub)|date=2020-02-06|author=[[Torsos]]}}</ref> The [[Chiefs Esports Club]] roster thus disbands.
|content5=
*January 25th - [[Chiefs Esports Club]] returns to the ''Rocket League'' scene by acquiring '''[[The Gospel of Lachlan]]'''. [[gus]], [[hntr]] and [[Superlachie]] join with [[LBP]] joining as coach.<ref name="chiefs 2024">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/ChiefsESC/status/1750429048365518907|title=The kings of OCE #RocketLeague return. Did you miss us @RLEsports? @gus__oce @hntrrlo @Superlachie_ @Coach_LBP|date=2024-01-25|author=[[Chiefs Esports Club]]}}</ref>
*April 14th - [[gus]] and [[Superlachie]] are released.<ref name="gus lachie">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/ChiefsESC/status/1779328748866990240|title=It was short but sweet, thank you @gus__oce & @Superlachierl. All the best in the future, we will see you on the field|date=2024-04-14|author=[[Chiefs Esports Club]]}}</ref>
*April 17th - [[finn]] and [[kaka]] join.<ref name="minions">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/chiefsesc/status/1780508736123175112|title=Let's get the ball rolling and bring in the minions @hntrrlo @kaka_rlo @rl_finn|date=2024-04-17|author=[[Chiefs Esports Club]]}}</ref>
*July 8th - [[finn]] retires.<ref name="finn">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/ChiefsESC/status/1810162404254523496|title=Thanks for the run @rl_finn Best of luck with life after Rocket League, enjoy retirement|author=[[Chiefs Esports Club]]|date=2024-07-08}}</ref>
*November 3rd - [[kaka]] leaves.<ref name="kaka out">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/AmphisR/status/1852972732679643184|title=We'd like to announce our new roster for the 2025 RLCS season, NewJeans:|date=2024-11-03|author=[[Amphis]]}}</ref>
*December 2nd - [[hntr]] and [[LBP]] are allowed to explore their options, leaving the active roster.<ref name="chfdrop">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/hntrrlo/status/1863524555781722156|title=Would love to stay with @ChiefsESC , but current restrictions put in place by epic are making it hard for them to stick around. Kindly they have allowed us to explore our options as they wait to see the feasibility of them keeping us on board. Contact us|date=2024-12-02|author=[[hntr]]}}</ref><ref name="chfdrop2">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/Fiberr_RL/status/1863522183076848015|title=Roster for RLCS 2025 Season|date=2024-12-02|author=[[Fibérr]]}}</ref>
|content6=
*January 9th - [[hntr]] and [[LBP]] return to the active roster, with [[Fibérr]] and [[Rezears]] joining to complete the roster.<ref name="chiefs25">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/chiefsesc/status/1877281081847579018|title=The landscape is changing, and so are we. In partnership with http://Helfie.ai we welcome the 2025 Helfie Chiefs @RLEsports roster: @hntrrlo @Fiberr_RL @rezears @Coach_LBP|date=2025-01-09|author=[[Chiefs Esports Club|Helfie Chiefs]]}}</ref>
*February 17th - [[FreaKii.]] joins as coach.<ref name="FreaKii">{{inside source}}</ref>
*July 3rd - [[hntr]], [[Fibérr]], [[Rezears]], [[LBP]] and [[FreaKii.]] are released.<ref name="release25">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/ChiefsESC/status/1940666828944298071|title=Some journeys go beyond wins and losses - Thank you for the memories, the fight, and for wearing the shield with pride. Wherever you go next, you'll always be a part of the family @hntrrlo @Fiberr_RL @rezears @Coach_LBP @FreaKiiRL|date=2025-07-03|author=[[Chiefs Esports Club|Helfie Chiefs]]}}</ref>
}}

