'''Team Falcons''' (formerly known as '''Falcons Esports''') is a [[:category:Saudi Arabia|Saudi Arabian]] esports organization which is currently hosting competitive teams in ''Apex Legends'', ''Arena of Valor'', ''Counter-Strike'', ''Dota 2'', ''EA Sports FC'', ''Fighting Games'', ''Fortnite'', ''Free Fire'', ''Honor of Kings'', ''Mobile Legends'', ''Overwatch'', ''PUBG'', ''PUBG Mobile'', ''Rainbow Six'', ''Rocket League'', ''Sim Racing'', ''StarCraft II'' and ''Teamfight Tactics''.<br>
The organization won the '''Esports World Cup Club Championship''' two times, in [[esports:Esports_World_Cup/2024|2024]] and [[esports:Esports_World_Cup/2025|2025]].

